# Same Supabase project as complex-recruitment-website.
#
# Every admin screen and the private document route run under the signed-in
# user's own session (RLS-enforced) and only ever need the two NEXT_PUBLIC_
# values below.
#
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY is the one exception: a narrowly-scoped, server-only
# privileged client (src/lib/supabase/admin.ts) uses it for Supabase Auth
# administration that genuinely requires service-role access — inviting a
# team member, resending an invitation, and activating an invited team
# member's own profile after they set their first password. It is never
# used for ordinary operational data (Jobs, Candidates, Applications, Staff
# Requests, Enquiries, Employers, Notes, Documents, Settings) — those
# continue to use RLS via the authenticated session. Never prefix this with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_, never import it into a Client Component, and set its real
# value only as a Secret environment variable in Vercel — never commit it.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
